1
00:00:00,917 --> 00:00:03,560
HumanCOIN. A dataset of human intent.

2
00:00:03,990 --> 00:00:05,904
Every demonstration records what happened;

3
00:00:06,347 --> 00:00:07,935
almost none record why.

4
00:00:08,990 --> 00:00:11,581
A demonstration is usually stored as a pair:

5
00:00:11,972 --> 00:00:14,407
an observation, and the action that followed.

6
00:00:14,837 --> 00:00:17,219
A policy learns to map one to the other.

7
00:00:17,662 --> 00:00:19,954
But the same observation can precede a lift,

8
00:00:20,201 --> 00:00:23,391
a re-grip, a pause, an abandoned attempt.

9
00:00:23,834 --> 00:00:25,266
The frame does not say which.

10
00:00:25,696 --> 00:00:27,441
Something is missing in between:

11
00:00:27,844 --> 00:00:30,994
the operator's intent, the state that decides how the

12
00:00:30,956 --> 00:00:33,196
action unfolds. It is latent.

13
00:00:33,626 --> 00:00:35,188
No camera sees it directly.

14
00:00:36,241 --> 00:00:38,416
Take something ordinary: picking up a cup.

15
00:00:38,845 --> 00:00:41,710
It takes a decision, a glance, and a movement.

16
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:44,601
Not three separate systems, one pathway.

17
00:00:45,030 --> 00:00:49,326
Cognition, vision, motor control, running from the decision to

18
00:00:49,275 --> 00:00:52,270
its effect. We call it the human intent pathway.

19
00:00:53,290 --> 00:00:56,168
The pathway is a complex system, but it leaves

20
00:00:56,181 --> 00:01:00,256
traces as it flows. Cortex prepares the movement hundreds

21
00:01:00,269 --> 00:01:03,797
of milliseconds before the hand moves, and EEG can

22
00:01:03,759 --> 00:01:07,808
see it. Muscle loads before contact, and surface EMG

23
00:01:07,821 --> 00:01:11,036
carries the load. Gaze reaches the object before the

24
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:13,380
fingers do, and eye tracking records it.

25
00:01:13,811 --> 00:01:15,842
Three stations. Three signals.

26
00:01:16,272 --> 00:01:16,923
One intent.

27
00:01:17,982 --> 00:01:20,612
This is the measurement HumanCOIN was built for.

28
00:01:21,042 --> 00:01:24,792
Twelve thousand five hundred hours, thirty-eight scene classes,

29
00:01:25,013 --> 00:01:28,243
and three tiers of intent proxies, on one task

30
00:01:28,256 --> 00:01:30,079
ontology and one clock.

31
00:01:31,108 --> 00:01:35,000
At the output end, L1: ten thousand hours of

32
00:01:34,884 --> 00:01:38,763
multi-view egocentric video, where gaze is inferred from the

33
00:01:38,621 --> 00:01:40,600
head camera before the hand departs.

34
00:01:41,043 --> 00:01:46,121
Midway, L2: two thousand hours, adding bilateral surface EMG,

35
00:01:46,460 --> 00:01:49,102
so load is readable before the object leaves the

36
00:01:48,986 --> 00:01:51,564
table. At the origin, L3:

37
00:01:51,955 --> 00:01:56,211
five hundred hours, adding scalp EEG, for preparation and

38
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:59,987
error monitoring. Each tier inherits every proxy below it.

39
00:02:00,353 --> 00:02:03,048
Depth is an axis, not a separate dataset.

40
00:02:04,106 --> 00:02:05,669
One episode, on one clock.

41
00:02:06,137 --> 00:02:08,169
Four head views and two wrist views.

42
00:02:08,598 --> 00:02:10,864
Depth and point cloud from the stereo pair.

43
00:02:11,307 --> 00:02:13,872
Six-degree-of-freedom head and wrist pose;

44
00:02:14,158 --> 00:02:15,734
twenty joint angles per hand.

45
00:02:16,163 --> 00:02:19,445
Gaze, EMG and EEG at their native rates.

46
00:02:19,874 --> 00:02:23,273
In the controlled L3 setting these quantities are measured,

47
00:02:23,663 --> 00:02:26,761
not inferred, a reference the shallower tiers can be

48
00:02:26,658 --> 00:02:27,479
scored against.

49
00:02:28,549 --> 00:02:30,242
The corpus is not one kind of room.

50
00:02:30,763 --> 00:02:33,432
Thirty-eight scene classes across five zones:

51
00:02:33,745 --> 00:02:37,143
residential, commercial, professional, industrial,

52
00:02:37,416 --> 00:02:40,958
public, plus residual. Ninety-nine task verbs.

53
00:02:41,401 --> 00:02:43,784
Six hundred and thirty-five object classes.

54
00:02:44,213 --> 00:02:46,245
A long tail, deliberately kept.

55
00:02:46,674 --> 00:02:49,422
The deeper the tier, the more controlled the staging:

56
00:02:49,851 --> 00:02:52,885
L3 is roughly seventy percent bench-controlled.

57
00:02:53,939 --> 00:02:55,997
Storage is asynchronous by design.

58
00:02:56,426 --> 00:02:59,447
Each stream keeps its own clock, its own native

59
00:02:59,460 --> 00:03:02,922
rate, and its own parquet table, twenty-three of them,

60
00:03:03,223 --> 00:03:06,659
never resampled. A master index at thirty frames per

61
00:03:06,635 --> 00:03:09,603
second resolves every modality at query time:

62
00:03:10,111 --> 00:03:12,937
nearest sample, interpolation, or a window.

63
00:03:13,379 --> 00:03:14,994
The data declares its alignment;

64
00:03:15,319 --> 00:03:16,361
it does not bake it in.

65
00:03:17,409 --> 00:03:20,858
HumanCOIN is led by B A A I, with

66
00:03:20,834 --> 00:03:24,323
twenty-seven institutions across universities and industry,

67
00:03:24,610 --> 00:03:26,328
and recordings from six sites.

68
00:03:27,341 --> 00:03:29,932
The data, the browser and the client are open.

69
00:03:30,362 --> 00:03:33,357
One command to install. One episode to begin.

70
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:36,755
Project page, report, and release are below.

71
00:03:37,185 --> 00:03:38,344
Welcome to HumanCOIN.
